Usages:
  conventions: .goga/usages/conventions.md

Annotations: |
  Apply `conventions` for code and test writing rules.

  This cell provides access to Markdown files within an indexed directory:
  file listing and content retrieval.

---

"Storage(directory_path: str)":
  location: storage.py
  annotations: |
    File storage. Captures the root directory on instantiation.

    `directory_path`: absolute path to the root directory containing Markdown files.

  methods:
    "list_files() -> files:list": |
      Recursively traverses the directory tree. Returns a list of relative paths
      for all .md files within directory_path.

      `files`: list of relative paths (e.g. ["docs/auth.md", "guide.md"]).

    "read_file(file_path: str) -> content:dict": |
      Reads file content by relative path within the indexed directory.

      `file_path`: relative path to the target file (e.g. "docs/auth.md").

      `content`: {"text": str, "source": str} — file text content and its absolute path.

      Raises FileNotFoundError if the file does not exist.
      The path must not escape the root directory boundary (path traversal protection).

